"Admission","href":"/en/parents/admission","text":"","context":"For Parents"},{"type":"page","title":"School Meals","href":"/en/parents/nutrition","text":"","context":"For Parents"},{"type":"page","title":"Parents' Committee","href":"/en/parents/committee","text":"","context":"For Parents"},{"type":"page","title":"FAQ","href":"/en/parents/faq","text":"","context":"For Parents"},{"type":"page","title":"Methodology","href":"/en/teachers/methodology","text":"","context":"For Teachers"},{"type":"page","title":"Professional Development","href":"/en/teachers/development","text":"","context":"For Teachers"},{"type":"page","title":"Early-Career Teachers","href":"/en/teachers/young-teachers","text":"","context":"For Teachers"},{"type":"page","title":"Pastoral Care Plan","href":"/en/upbringing/plan","text":"","context":"Pastoral Care"},{"type":"page","title":"Psychological Service","href":"/en/upbringing/psychologist","text":"","context":"Pastoral Care"},{"type":"page","title":"Social Pedagogue","href":"/en/upbringing/social-pedagogue","text":"","context":"Pastoral Care"},{"type":"page","title":"Offence Prevention","href":"/en/upbringing/prevention","text":"","context":"Pastoral Care"},{"type":"page","title":"Child Safety","href":"/en/upbringing/safety","text":"","context":"Pastoral Care"},{"type":"page","title":"Anti-Corruption Education","href":"/en/upbringing/anti-corruption","text":"","context":"Pastoral Care"},{"type":"page","title":"National and Educational Projects","href":"/en/upbringing/projects","text":"","context":"Pastoral Care"},{"type":"page","title":"Funding","href":"/en/budget/funding","text":"","context":"Open Budget"},{"type":"page","title":"Financial Reports","href":"/en/budget/reports","text":"","context":"Open Budget"},{"type":"page","title":"Documents","href":"/en/budget/documents","text":"","context":"Open Budget"},{"type":"page","title":"Public Procurement","href":"/en/budget/procurement","text":"","context":"Open Budget"},{"type":"page","title":"Catering","href":"/en/budget/nutrition","text":"","context":"Open Budget"},{"type":"page","title":"Public Information","href":"/en/budget/public","text":"","context":"Open Budget"},{"type":"page","title":"Regulations","href":"/en/official/regulations","text":"","context":"Official Information"},{"type":"page","title":"State Symbols","href":"/en/official/symbols","text":"The state symbols of the Republic of Kazakhstan are the State Flag, the State Emblem and the State Anthem. State Flag The State Flag is a rectangular sky-blue cloth with a radiant sun in the centre and a soaring steppe eagle beneath it. A vertical band of national ornament runs along the hoist. It was adopted on 4 June 1992. Designer: Shaken Niyazbekov. State Emblem The State Emblem is circular and shows a shanyrak (the crown of a yurt) on a sky-blue background, with uyks radiating from it like rays of the sun. Mythical winged horses are placed on both sides. It was adopted on 4 June 1992. Designers: Zhandarbek Malibekov and Shot-Aman Ualikhanov. State Anthem Since 7 January 2006 the State Anthem has been the song “Menin Qazaqstanym”. Music by Shamshi Kaldayakov; lyrics by Zhumeken Nazhimedenov and Nursultan Nazarbayev. The status and use of the state symbols are governed by the Constitutional Law “On the State Symbols of the Republic of Kazakhstan”. 4 June is State Symbols Day.","context":"Official Information"},{"type":"page","title":"Public Services","href":"/en/official/services","text":"","context":"Official Information"},{"type":"page","title":"Self-Assessment","href":"/en/official/self-assessment","text":"","context":"Official Information"},{"type":"page","title":"Attestation","href":"/en/official/attestation","text":"","context":"Official Information"},{"type":"page","title":"Administrative Documents","href":"/en/official/admin-documents","text":"","context":"Official Information"},{"type":"page","title":"Vacancies","href":"/en/official/vacancies","text":"","context":"Official Information"},{"type":"news","title":"The school's new website is live","href":"/en/news/new-website","text":"The official school website has been renewed: three languages, clear navigation and a mobile version. The school's new official website is now live. It works in Kazakh, Russian and English, is easy to use on smartphones and includes a low-vision version. The site is currently being filled with content. The school administration will publish information in each section step by step.","context":""}]